    "notes": "Sesotho (Southern Sotho) uses a Latin QWERTY alphabet; a clean QWERTY base is appropriate. The letter s-caron (š), used in some orthographic conventions, is added as a direct key on the home row; its position is best-effort and to be verified against branah. Digraphs such as tj, tlh, kh and ny are typed as letter sequences."
